    "explanation": "Arbitrary bijections of symbol labels need not respect XOR translations, so they cannot generally be implemented by the asserted fixed conjugation around a single oracle call.",
    "evidence": "Take three-bit symbols and a bijection phi that swaps 1 and 2 and fixes 0,3,4,5,6,7. Fixed before/after value-register unitaries implementing every relabeled oracle, with phi(0)=0, would conjugate X_a to X_phi(a), where X_a|b>=|b XOR a>. Since X_a X_b=X_(a XOR b), this requires phi(a XOR b)=phi(a) XOR phi(b). But phi(1 XOR 4)=phi(5)=5, whereas phi(1) XOR phi(4)=2 XOR 4=6. Querying into an ancilla, applying phi, updating the response, and uncomputing uses two oracle calls; constant-factor asymptotic transfers may survive.",
